## 📝 Examples

### ✅ Correct Usage

```tsx
// Using global colors
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border">
  <Button variant="healthcare">Submit</Button>
  <Card variant="healthcareSuccess">Success message</Card>
</div>

// Using opacity modifiers
<div className="bg-primary/10 text-primary border-primary/20">
  Primary content
</div>
```

### ❌ Incorrect Usage

```tsx
// Hardcoded colors - FORBIDDEN
<div className="bg-blue-50 text-gray-900 border-green-200">
  <button className="bg-blue-500 text-white">Submit</button>
</div>

// Hardcoded gradients - FORBIDDEN
<div className="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-purple-600">
  Content
</div>
```

## 🚀 Implementation

This rule ensures:

- **Consistent healthcare branding** across all components
- **Proper theming** for light and dark modes
- **Maintainable code** with centralized color management
- **Professional appearance** suitable for healthcare applications
- **Accessibility compliance** with proper contrast ratios

**Remember**: When in doubt, always use the global color system defined in `globals.css`!
